# Build context for the API image, which is the repository root because the
# image has to carry `bots/` — see the header of `apps/api/Dockerfile`.
#
# Only builds whose *context* is this directory read this file, so the worker
# and bot-desktop images keep using their own `.dockerignore` unchanged.
#
# Deny by default, then re-admit exactly what the image needs. Without this the
# daemon uploads the whole monorepo on every build — `.git`, `node_modules`,
# `apps/desktop/src-tauri/target`, `data/bot-homes` — none of which is COPYed
# and all of which invalidates nothing useful. Deny-first also means a file
# added later (a dump, a notebook full of credentials, an `.env`) cannot reach
# the context by accident.
*

!apps/api/requirements.txt
!apps/api/requirements-dev.txt
!apps/api/app/
!apps/api/sql/
!apps/api/alembic.ini
!apps/api/alembic/
# The reason this context is the repo root: the five system-bot prompts.
!bots/

# Re-exclude the noise inside the admitted directories: negation patterns do
# not recurse into what a later rule re-excludes, so these must come last.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.ipynb_checkpoints/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.log
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.db
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/tests/
